# Syanat — Security & Cost Audit Report

> **Audit Type:** Read-only  
> **Auditor:** Senior Application Security & Firebase Review  
> **Scope:** All Dart source files in `lib/`, `firestore.rules`, `storage.rules`  
> **Date:** 2026-04-04  

---

## Executive Summary

The application is **generally well-structured** and contains several good practices already in place (server-side timestamps, `FieldValue.increment`, transaction-gated status machines, duplicate-submit guards, receipt total recomputation). However, there are **several real-world exploitable gaps** that must be closed before a production launch. The most critical issues are in Firestore Rules authorization where the **new job status flow (technician_accepted → technician_arrived → work_finished → awaiting_customer_approval → receipt_disputed) is entirely absent from the server-side rules**, making all those transitions bypassable or blockable by any client-side manipulation.

