## Section 4 — Firebase Billing / Cost Leaks

### 🟠 HIGH — B4-01: `streamTechnicianUnreadNotifCount` Reads All Unread Docs Instead of Aggregating

**File:** `lib/firebase_service.dart` (L1402–1410)  
```dart
static Stream<int> streamTechnicianUnreadNotifCount(String techId) {
    return firestore
        .collection('notifications')
        .where('technicianId', isEqualTo: techId)
        .where('read', isEqualTo: false)
        .limit(100)
        .snapshots()
        .map((snap) => snap.docs.length);  // ← Reads 100 docs to count
}
```
A badge counter is subscribed as a live stream on the tech home screen. This reads up to 100 document payloads on every listener attach and on every change to any notification. For notification badges, only the `count()` is needed.

**Impact:** If a technician has 100 unread notifications, every badge update costs 100 document reads instead of 1 aggregation query.

**Fix Required:** Use `count()` aggregation:
```dart
.where('read', isEqualTo: false).count().get()
```
Note: aggregations cannot be streamed natively; poll on a timer or use a Cloud Function to maintain a counter field.

